    "type": "assistant_message",
    "content": "All 19 checklist items have been executed and recorded — coverage is complete.\n\n**Summary: 17 PASS / 2 FAIL**\n\nThe core to-do functionality is solid: creation with full details, editing, deletion, completion, active/completed view switching with accurate counts, priority and deadline sorting (undated tasks last), blocked-task distinction, prerequisite warnings, cycle prevention (direct *and* indirect), and both hover tooltips (dashed connector and blocked warning) all behave as specified.\n\nTwo defects found:\n\n- **FT-3 — Blocked tasks are entirely uneditable.** The requirement is that a blocked task still allows description and priority changes while locking title and deadline. In practice the whole edit button is `disabled`, and no alternate affordance exists (clicking the title or priority badge does nothing), so the two fields that should remain editable are not.\n\n- **CS-22 — Invalid completed+blocked state.** Reopening a prerequisite whose dependent was already completed is permitted, and the dependent stays `completed` while simultaneously showing \"Prerequisite ... incomplete\". Worse, its complete toggle and edit button are both disabled, so the task is stranded in an unrecoverable state — the system neither blocks the reopen nor cascades the dependent back to incomplete.\n\nOne methodology note worth flagging: for IX-18 I had to dispatch pointer events programmatically rather than use a normal hover, because the dashed connector is a purely vertical SVG path with a 0px-wide bounding box. The tooltip logic itself works correctly, but that zero-width hit area may make the connection genuinely hard to hover for real users despite the 16px-wide transparent hit path."
  }
}
